Perfect! All tests now pass. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which caused it to:
1. Return the second word instead of the first word in 'hello world'
2. Throw an IndexError when there was only a single word

I fixed it by changing `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and now both tests pass successfully.
